WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.030
I come from a family that loved theater.

2
00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:05.480
And I love the mistakes, I love the messiness,

3
00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.210
I love the seams.

4
00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:09.370
But I've always been afraid, if I ever did theater

5
00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:10.940
and I made a mistake or I messed up,

6
00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.010
what would happen?

7
00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:15.160
Have you ever had an experience in the theater like that?

8
00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.540
And if so, what did you do,

9
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.629
and what would your advice... ?

10
00:00:17.629 --> 00:00:18.780
Well, I don't even know where to start.

11
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:19.650
Right?
(audience laughs)

12
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:23.510
I mean, essentially, 25 years

13
00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:25.620
in London and here,

14
00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:29.432
I mean, I've been set fire to in mid-air on wires.

15
00:00:29.432 --> 00:00:30.265
(Drew laughs)

16
00:00:30.265 --> 00:00:31.990
In Andrew Lloyd-Webber's "The Wizard of Oz,"

17
00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:33.932
that we did at the London Palladium,

18
00:00:33.932 --> 00:00:37.460
I had like, a finger flash fire

19
00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:40.968
that would launch at the Scarecrow, as you do.

20
00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:42.400
(audience laughs)
Down on the deck.

21
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:43.340
And set fire to him.

22
00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:44.750
He'd set off something.

23
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:48.400
But my costume was completely black, inky feathers.

24
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.907
And the finger flash didn't go off.

25
00:00:50.907 --> 00:00:52.570
"Oh boy," indeed.
(audience laughs)

26
00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:55.860
And I moved my hand back onto the broomstick,

27
00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.140
and my whole dress went on fire.

28
00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:00.420
What did you do?

29
00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:01.408
I went.

30
00:01:01.408 --> 00:01:03.280
(audience laughs)
Mid-air.

31
00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.728
And how funny is this?

32
00:01:04.728 --> 00:01:06.580
That very day,

33
00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:08.540
my beloved friend Clay Aiken

34
00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:10.650
was in the audience watching me,

35
00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.756
and was like.
(Hannah screams)

36
00:01:12.756 --> 00:01:13.690
(audience laughs)

37
00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:16.000
Hey, hold on, broomstick.

38
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:16.910
Witch.

39
00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.070
Don't get me started.

40
00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:21.145
You are in the new "Hocus Pocus."

41
00:01:21.145 --> 00:01:24.136
(audience cheers)

42
00:01:24.136 --> 00:01:25.876
I'm freaking out!

43
00:01:25.876 --> 00:01:27.293
I'm freaking out!

44
00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:34.430
This movie is so meaningful and important to so many people.

45
00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:36.400
Sam Richardson was here the other day.

46
00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.560
Sam Richardson who is in "Ted Lasso" as well!

47
00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.560
That's right!
Oh my God!

48
00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.560
And so I grilled him about it.

49
00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:43.760
Oh my gosh, it's immense.

50
00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:44.830
What is it like?

51
00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:46.530
I would have paid them for the privilege.

52
00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:47.530
But don't tell them that.
(audience laughs)

53
00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:51.200
So I arrived for my costume fitting in Rhode Island,

54
00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.357
and the second AD was like,

55
00:01:53.357 --> 00:01:55.290
"The ladies would love to meet you."

56
00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:56.567
And I was like, "The...?"

57
00:01:57.957 --> 00:01:59.157
The ladies.

58
00:01:59.157 --> 00:02:00.540
"Them? The witchy ladies?"

59
00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:01.373
And he was like,

60
00:02:01.373 --> 00:02:02.377
"Yeah, they're just finishing up on a scene,

61
00:02:02.377 --> 00:02:03.490
"but if you'd like to come to set..."

62
00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:04.323
And I was like,

63
00:02:05.377 --> 00:02:06.590
"Yes, please."

64
00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:07.960
And got driven there,

65
00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.890
and they came off set,

66
00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:12.640
and there were Dame Bette, Kathy,

67
00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:14.138
and SJP sitting there.

68
00:02:14.138 --> 00:02:17.180
(audience cheers)
Having their lunch.

69
00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:19.950
In a little box like we all do on set.

70
00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.916
In their costumes.

71
00:02:21.916 --> 00:02:23.070
It was just like...

72
00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:25.277
And I said, "I just wanted to quickly come

73
00:02:25.277 --> 00:02:26.540
"and say hello."

74
00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.584
And Bette,

75
00:02:28.584 --> 00:02:29.417
Bette.

76
00:02:29.417 --> 00:02:30.289
(audience laughs)

77
00:02:30.289 --> 00:02:31.450
Was just like, "Come, come and sit."

78
00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:32.283
And I was like, "No, no, no, no,

79
00:02:32.283 --> 00:02:33.787
"you're having your time, I get it.

80
00:02:33.787 --> 00:02:34.977
"I know it's down time."

81
00:02:34.977 --> 00:02:36.470
"No, no, no, come and sit with us."

82
00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:38.610
And they were just

83
00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:40.570
so delicious.

84
00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:41.850
And

85
00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.957
Bette was just like, "Well played.

86
00:02:43.957 --> 00:02:45.110
"Well played for this year."

87
00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:45.997
And I thought,
(audience gasps)

88
00:02:45.997 --> 00:02:48.497
"I can't even believe you know I exist.

89
00:02:48.497 --> 00:02:49.330
"I can't cope with it."

90
00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:51.890
It was just insane.
(audience cheers)

91
00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:53.973
It is absolutely, right?

92
00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:54.857
She is something.

93
00:02:54.857 --> 00:02:58.140
And my daughter is obsessed with the film.

94
00:02:58.140 --> 00:02:59.822
Especially Kathy Najimy with-

95
00:02:59.822 --> 00:03:01.050
(Hannah makes indistinct sounds)

96
00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.480
I mean, it's "Hocus Pocus,"

97
00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:04.380
I've seen it probably a hundred times.

98
00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:05.490
I'm so excited.

99
00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:06.840
I'm so excited for this gift.

100
00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.410
We all need this like "Ted Lasso,"

101
00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:09.468
we're all gonna be like.

102
00:03:09.468 --> 00:03:10.680
"Mmm, yum, yum, yum."
Yes, yes!

103
00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.690
Okay, there's one other character

104
00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:14.270
that I have to talk to you about.

105
00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:16.068
Is it true...

106
00:03:16.068 --> 00:03:17.050
(Hannah cackles)

107
00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.430
That you are

108
00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:22.330
the nun in "Game of Thrones"

109
00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:23.163
I am.

110
00:03:23.163 --> 00:03:25.490
Who literally says the famous phrase?

111
00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:26.470
Shame!

112
00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.213
(audience cheers)
Yes!

113
00:03:29.202 --> 00:03:32.967
I am!
(Hannah laughs)

114
00:03:32.967 --> 00:03:34.800
So don't screw up.

115
00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:37.070
Otherwise I'll get you with my bell.

116
00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:38.820
I've got my bell.

117
00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:40.040
Did you save it?

118
00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:41.000
I've got my bell.

119
00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.665
That's when you know that you're dead.

120
00:03:42.665 --> 00:03:44.260
(audience laughs)
On the show.

121
00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:47.770
'Cause they're like, "Here you are, here is your hero prop."

122
00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:48.700
There we go.

123
00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.140
I had breakfast with Miss Headey this morning.

124
00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:51.973
No way!

125
00:03:51.973 --> 00:03:53.563
Yeah, oh, we're in love with each other.

126
00:03:53.563 --> 00:03:54.396
Wait a minute!

127
00:03:54.396 --> 00:03:55.930
We love each other!

128
00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:57.837
I don't know what I want more to picture,

129
00:03:57.837 --> 00:04:02.060
"Hocus Pocus 2" and you and SJP and Kathy Najimy

130
00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.960
and the divine Miss M,

131
00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:07.820
or that you and Lena Headey were literally like...

132
00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:11.057
I had scrambled eggs this morning.

133
00:04:11.057 --> 00:04:14.014
(audience cheers)

134
00:04:14.014 --> 00:04:15.681
We are great pals.

135
00:04:15.681 --> 00:04:18.264 line:15%
(upbeat music)

